# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docker build context exclusions.
# Only these are COPYed into the image (see Dockerfile):
#   bin/ app/ config/ videos/ web/
# Everything else is stripped to keep the build context small and to
# keep secrets / local artifacts out of the image layers.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

# Version control & CI
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore
.github
.gitattributes

# Secrets, local env files & certificates
.env
.env.*
*.env
*.crt
*.key
*.pem
auto.crt
auto.key

# Python runtime artifacts
__pycache__
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# Docs & developer-only files (not needed at runtime)
*.md
LICENSE
docs/

# Compose / local tooling
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.yaml
test_client.py
.gitlab-ci.yml
Makefile

# Editors, OS & IDE cruft
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
*.log
logs/
*.pid

# HLS segments & temporary streaming dumps (generated at runtime)
*.ts
*.m4s
*.m3u8
*.mpd
recordings/
test_output/
snapshot_*.png

# NOTE: videos/ and bin/ are intentionally NOT ignored.
#   videos/ holds the CCTV sample footage the container streams.
#   bin/mediamtx avoids re-downloading the binary on every build.
